        <p>Mr. Alan Sykes, Ml'., in seconding,said Sir Gilbert', name was known throughout the agricultural world. They were all glad to see him included in the Corona- tion honours—(applattse)—the only thing they could quarrel about would be thkt the hcuour was not sufficiently high. The vote was heartily accorded. . . .</p>
