      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-08-19_WidnesExaminer_art0024" n="art0024">
        <head>HOME RULE CAMPAIGN.</head>
        <p>HOME RULE CAMPAIGN.</p>
        <p>Liberals Forming a Powerful Organization.</p>
        <p>A powerful organizstion is being formed by th• Liberal potty for propagendt work in csnneltion with Home Rule. A large number of M.P.'s have already offered their services in connection with the campaign. Mr. Winston Conrchill has consested to become the chairman of a small executive csmmittee,of which Mr. Robert Harcourt, M P., will be the bon secretary. Mr. Donald McLean, M.P., who, with Mr. liercourto has had very considerable experience in organi- zation work, will be the hon. treasurer. it is probable that Mr. Wallace Carter, organising secretary of the Free Trade Union, will become general secretary of the new organisation. Mr. .1. M. Robertaon, M.P., has agreed to look after the literory department, and it is probable that be will co-operate with other well-known writers in this work. A very active campaign will be commenced in oho early autumn. Mr. Harcourt is making arrangements to open special of9com, and in due course will plot* him- self in communication with Literal ativociatioss throughout the comotry. Pending the opening of the offices csminunicationa in reference to the movement rbould be addrasied to Mr. Harcourt at the House of Commons.</p>
        <p>A branch of the society is to be started in Scotland, with Mr. Ganand, as organising secretary.</p>
        <p>CB for Cakes, Pastry, Puddings &amp; Pies. ORWICK S BAKING POWDER.</p>
