        <p>District Champion Cup (presented by Sir Gilbert Greenall) for the best mare or* filly : J Gould; r, W Cunningham. Silver Cup (presented by Sir Gilbert Greenall) for best shire exhibit in tenant class : A Broome; r, Exors of John Blackshaw. Special prize (presented by Mr P Stapleton Bretherton) for beat shire filly : W Cnnoinghatu ; r J Gould. Silver Cup (prsented by Mr John Coxon) for best shire blood mare, the property of a tenant farmer : J Gould. Three best shire foals sired by any of Mr Whittaker Kenworthy's horses T Johnson, Wimbody Tafford ; J Warburton, Grappenhall ; S Blythe, Alvanlev. Three best shire foals by any of Mr J Goulds horses : A Platt : R Clarke ; A E Ward, Mobberley. Three hest colt foals and tbeir filly foals by "Admiral Bosco " : B Billington, S Billington, Stratton W Blackshavv, T Percival, Warringto3 ; T Warburton. Darestury. Stlver cup for best dairy cow : S S Raingill. Silver cup for best heifer, the property of a tenant farmer: S W Gould. Prizes offered by Messrs Day nod Sons, Crewe, for best cattle exhibits, by a tenant farmer : S S Raingill. Prizes offered by NI esars Henry Milling 6; Co., Ltd., for best white cheese: G Platt. Gold medal offered by Shire Horse Society for best mare or filly (members' classes) : J Gould. Silver medals offered by Hunters' Improvement Society for best hunter filly and mare or gelding : J W Farish and R Needham. Silver medals offered by Hackey Horse Society for best hackney or pony mare, filly with ally foal mare or gelding : A J Willett, S L Kappell.</p>
