        <p>- DISTRICT CLASSES.—Brood More having produced a living foal by, or in foal to, a thoroughbred or registered banter sire in 1911. First prize, £5 : second, £3 ; third, £2 : 1, Robert Needham, Reston Lodge, Knutsford ; 2, Joseph Millington, S ,tton Hall, Kinderton, Middlewich ; 3, Ernest Griffiths, Broken Cross, Northwich ; riMsjor .1 E Groves, Dean's Green Lymm. Foal by al thoroughbred or registered hunter sire.—First prize, £4 ; second, £3; third, £2 ; fourth, £1: 1, Ernest Griffiths, Broken Cross, Northwich ; 2, Robert Needham, Beaton Lodge, Knutsford ; 3, Major J E G Groves, Dean's Green, Lymm ; 4, John W Farish, Marston Hall, Northwich. Yearling colt, gelding or filly by a thoroughbred registered hunter sire.—First prize, £4 ; 'second, £3 ; third, ,E 2 : 1, William H Shiers, Too Red Howie, Hart- ford; 2, John W Farish,Marston 1101,Northwich. Two- year-old gelding or filly by a thoroughbred or registered hunter sire.—First prize, .£4 ; second, £3 ; third, £2 : 1, Ernest Griffiths, Broken Cross,Northwich ; 2, Robert Needham, Beaton Lodge,Knotsford ; 3, John W Farish, Marston Hall, Northwich. Three-year-old gelding or Elly by a thoroughbred or registered hunter sire.— First prize, Li; second prize, £3 ; third, £2: 1, Ernest Griffith, Broken Cross, Northwich ; 2 and 3, John W Fairish, Marston Hall, Northwich. OPEN CLASSES (To be ridden).—Novice hunter mare or gelding, 4 years old and upwards, equal to carry 13 stone and not more than list. 7lbs. No entry in this class has ever been awarded a prize of £lO or over in a riding class at any show previous to August Bth, 1911. —First prize, £l5 ; second, £lO ; third, £5 ; fourth,E3 : I, J H Stokes, Great 11,wden. Market Herhorough ; 2,William Gale,Weltham,filelton Mowbray ; 3, Countess of Warwick, Easton Lodge, Dunmow, Eases : 4, Jersey de Kooop, Calveley Hall, Tarporley ; r, John Drage, Chapel Brampton, Northampton. Novice bunter mare or gelding, 4 years old and upwards equal to carry over 14s. 7lba. .No entry