        <p>DtsTim,. Ccasses.—Brood 1111f11, having produced a living fool by, or in foal to, a ragiatered hackney eireiin</p>
        <p>1911.—First prize, £5 ; second, £3 ; third, £2: 1, John Makeague, Go!borne Park, Newton-le-Willowa ; 2, William Johnson, Acrefieid Stod, Woolton ; 3, Whittaker and Oliver, Agden, Lymm; r, James B Aitken, Hall Nook, Penketh ; h c, Alfred Broome, Windmill Farm, Preston B ouk. Foal by a registered hackney sire.—First prize, .C 3 ; second, £2 ; third. £ : 1, Alfred Broome, Windmill Farm, Preston Brook ; 2, Whittaker and Oliver, A gden, Lymm ; 3, Anthony Garnett, Spring Farm, Tarbock ; r, Thomas Warburton. Hall-lane Farm, Daresbury. Yearling colt, gelding or filly, by a registered leickney sire—First prize, £4 ; second, £3 ; third, £2 : 1, Alfred Smith. Inglewood, Windle, St. Helens ; 2, C Stanley Smith, Heath Bootee, Croft ; 3, E K Richardson, Dakinfleld Hail, Itiobberley; r, Anthony Garnett, Spring Farm, Yarbock. Two-year- old gelding or filly by a registered hackney sire.—First prize, £4; second prize, £3 ; third prize, £2: 1, Joshua Ball, Santworth Hall, Warrington ; 2, William Johnson, Acrefleld Stud, Wootton ; 3, Whittaker and Oliv,r, Agden, Lymm ; r, Richard Billington, Brook- side Farm, Stratton ; ho, W Worthiogton, Bairn. Barn Earm, Mere. Three-ye tr-old gelding or lllly by a registered hackney sire.—First prize, .£1; second, £3 ; third £2.1, John Makeague, Golborne Park,Newtonite- Willows ; 2 Joshua Ball, Southworth Hell, Warrington; 3, William Worthington, Hulme Barn Farm, Mere; ru James B ARken,Hall Nook. Penketh. Pony brood, mare, not exceeding 14 hands, having produced a Briny foal by, or in foal to, a registered hackney, or registered hackney pony stallion in 1911—First prize, £5 second prize, £3 ; third prize £2. 1, Arthur J Whitecroft, Stockton Ilyatla ; 2, Edward L Bent, The Vulcan. Newton-le-Willows ; 3, J B Egerton, Lymm. Foal by a registered hackney, or registered hackney pony stallion, out of a mare entered in class 23.—First £3; second, £2; third, £1 :1, Joshua II Southworth Hall, Warrington : 2, Arthur J Willett, White. croft, Stockton Heath ; 3, Edward L Bent, The Vulcan, Newton-le-Willows ; r, J B Egortan, Lyrists</p>
