      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-08-19_WidnesExaminer_art0061" n="art0061">
        <head>HARNESS CLASSES.</head>
        <p>HARNESS CLASSES.</p>
        <p>OPEN CLASSES.—Novice mare or gelding not exceed- ing 14 bands. No entry in this class tan ever been awarded a prize in harness exceeding the value of £5 at any show (males and tradesmen's classes excepted) previous to Stli Anaust,l9ll.—First prize, RIO; second, £5 ; third, £3 : 1, Howard Frank, Rusthall, Wimbledon Common ; 2, John French, 112, Liverpool-road, St. Helens; 3, Edward Holmts and Sons, Ash Cottage, Stratton ; r, C E Tunnicliffe, Platt House, Deganary. Novice mare or gelding, over 14 and not exceeding 15 bands. No entry in this dens has ever been awarded a prize in harness exceeding the value if ,E 5 at any show (sales and tradesmen's classes excepted) previous to Bth August, 1911.—First prize, £10; second, £5 ; third, £3: 1, C E Tunnicliffe, Plst House, Deganwy ; 2, Howard Frank, Rustball, Wimbledon Common ; 3, T Stephenson, Derby-road, Huyton ; r, Thomas Catlow, Higher Trap Stud, Padiham. Novice mare or gelding exceeding 15 hands. No entry in this class has ever been awarded a prize in harness exceeding the value of £5 at any show (sale, and tradesmen's chtsses excepted) previous to Bth August, 1211.—First prize, EH): second, £5 ; third, £3 : 1, S L Eappel, Berlin, Germany ; 2, Mrs 51 Hignett, OMey Ley, Crewe ; 3, Slits Dora Schintz, Childwall Hall, Liverpool ; r, John Makeague, Golborne Park, Newton-le-Willows. TRADESMEN'S OR TENANT FARMERS' TURNOUTS.</p>
        <p>DISTRICT CLASSES.—Light horses (single Of pair vehicle and harness.—First prize, £5 ; secon4,£3; third £2 ; fourth, £1: 1, Edward Holmes and Sons, Ash Cottage, Stratton ; 2, William Johnson, butcher, Lymm ; 3, T 51 Stephenson, Derby-road, Huyton ; 4, George Brown, 94, Duke-street, St. Helena ; r, John Wilson, 4, Denton's Green-lane, St. Helens. Vanners or light lorry horses (single or pair) vehicle and lisrnass.—First prize, £5 ; sec mi. £3; third,El; fourth, £1 : I, Edward Monks, 51 and 53, Bridge-street, Run- corn ; 2, Thomas Warhurton,Hall-lane Faroi,Daresburs; 3, S Carter and Co., corn merchants, Mersey-street, Warrington ; 4, Chently and Soo, 13, Sankey-street, Warrington ; r, James C Naylor, 110, Winwick-road, Warrington. Single heavy horse, vehicle and harness, belonging to a tradesman.—First prize, £5, second, £3; third, £2; fourth, LI: 1, Peter Wright, Sutton-road Farm, Rainhill ; 2, Warrington Co-operative Society, Limited. Warrington ; 3, George lloward, 2, Bsnnett- street, Warrington. Single heavy horse, vehicle and harness, belonging to a tersest farmer. No horse in this class has ever been awordet a first prize stony sho (sales excepted) in 1910 or 1911.—First prize,£s;sesond, £3; third, £2 ; fourth, £1 : 2, Alfred Broome,W indrnil I Farm, Preston Brook ; 3, It I. Warburton, Ilstten ; 4, J K Prieatrier, Porch House Farm, Acton Grange ; r Thomas Morris, Marsh House Farm, Dutton.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-08-19_WidnesExaminer_art0062" n="art0062">
        <head>CAT CLE.</head>
        <p>CAT CLE.</p>
        <p>DI,TRICT CLAS,ES.—Dairy cow In calf (to calve within 2 months after date of abow).—First prize, £1 ; second, £3 ; third, £2 : 1, Sam S Raineill,The Grange, Ringway. Altriocham ; 2 and 3, Sam W Gould, Foaley Hall, Lvmm ; r and h c, William Worthington, Hu!me Barn Farm, Mere. Dairy cow in milk.—First prizv, £1 ; reaond, £3 ; third, £2 : 1, Sam S Raingili, The Grange, Ringway, Altrincham ; 2, William Worthington, Hulme Barn Farm, Mere ; 3, Thomas Warburton, Hall Line Farm, Daresbury. Heifer under 3 years.—First prize, £1; second, £3 ; third, £2 : 1, William Cooper, Clayton's Farm, Burton- wood, near Newton-le-Willows ; 2, Thomas Billington, Newton Bank Farm, Preston Brook ; 3, Sam W Gould, Finley Hall, Lymm ; r, Arthur Platt, Wincham, near Northvrich. Helfer under 2 years.—Firat prize, £4 ; second, £3 ; third, £2 : 1 and 2, Sam W Gould, Foxley Hall, Lymm ; 3, Richard Clarke, Warburton Park; r, Mrs Frances Cowart, Bowling Green, Little Leigh. 1131 I under 2 years.—Farst prize, £5 ; second, £3 ; third, £2 . I, Sam S Raingill, The Grange, Ringway, Altrinchara ; 2, Thomas Eden, Park House Farm Keats- ford 3, C L Agnew, The Pole, Northwich ; r, Richard Clarke Warburton Park. Bull, over 2 yeara.—First prize, £5 ; second, £3 ; third, £2 : I, Sam W Gould, Foxley HalliLymna ; 2, H L Warburton, Hatton ;3, Exors John,Blackshaw, Blue Coat Farm, Hatton.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-08-19_WidnesExaminer_art0063" n="art0063">
        <head>PIGS.</head>
        <p>PIGS.</p>
        <p>DISTRICT CLASSES.—Breeding now in pig, or with litter, any age or hreed.—Pirst prize, £3 : second, £2; third, El : 1, J M Newton, Birch Farm, IVaiburton ; 2, wl4 Carter, Moss Hall, Carrington, Manchester; Pimlott, Queen's Buildings, Altrincham ;r, T H Fairhurst, Hatton, near Warrington. Lest gilt (any breed) born in 1911.—First prize, £3; second, £2; third £1 : I, J 11 Newton, Birch Perm, Warburton ; 2, W 11 Carter, Moss Hall, Carrington, Manchester ; 3, .1 Al Newton, Birch Farm, Warburton ; r, G Pimlott, Queen's Buildings, Altrinchsm. Best boar (any breed), born in 1911.—First pare, £3; second, £2; third, £1: 1, G Pimlott, Queen's Buildings, Altrincbarn ; 2, W H Carter Moss Hall, Csirington Manchester ;3, J Newton, Birch P..nu, Wsrbureou ; r, Thomas Moore, Lime Cottage, Oughtrington-lan., Lymm. Best Cottager's pig.—Prat prize, £2 ; second, El ; third, Wu.: 1, and 2, William Ball, Hatton, near Warrington ; CHEESE.</p>
