      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-08-19_WidnesExaminer_art0100" n="art0100">
        <head>Examiner Saturday August 19, 1911 LEGAL FIRST AID. I</head>
        <p>The Examiner Saturday August 19, 1911 LEGAL FIRST AID. I</p>
        <p>diphtheria and with 10 cases of scarlet fever all their beds were exhausted. Ile thought something &amp;natio should be done. Mr. Chadwick remarked that there were 20 cuee of diphtheria in Weston. Dr. Adams said that he would go over to Weston. Fie thought the great number of cases were corned by personal infection—children playing with others.</p>
